    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d446">

                <pb facs="0433" n="423" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg423"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.2531/230: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Chile</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Frost</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-08T11:00:00-04:00">December 8, 1937—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 8—10:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>89. Department’s 55, December 2, 4 p.m. Foreign Office here approved
                    interpretation of item (<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) contained in my telegram
                        80;<anchor n="46" xml:id="d446-f1"/> but García at Buenos Aires, to whom it
                    was air mailed, has unexpectedly raised objections to fourth sentence, regarding
                    recourse to <pb facs="0434" n="424" xml:id="pg424"/> import quotas. A
                    modification of this sentence may be submitted to the Department by telegraph
                    tomorrow. García’s return now set for early next week.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Frost</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
